  text: 'Create a X3DOM edge integration and mobile scene asset for the 3d-engines-and-webgl category. Scenario: A responsive React or plain HTML embed with explicit x3d sizing, x3dom.reload for dynamic markup, touch examine navigation, and missing CSS warning. Use declarative X3D embedded in HTML using x3d, scene, viewpoint, navigationInfo, shapes, appearances, materials, ROUTE, and runtime API. Build an edge-case integration scene that emphasizes responsive layout, mobile or touch controls, fallback behavior, loading errors, and embedding constraints. The generated artifact must include a visible nonblank initial render, a deliberately framed starting camera, solution-appropriate lighting and materials, at least one animation or user interaction, explicit asset loading or placeholder handling, and mobile/performance notes in code comments or UI diagnostics. Return complete source for the requested artifact without markdown fences or explanatory prose outside the source.'
  requirements:
  - Start from a nonblank render state; do not rely on a user action before the first visible frame.
  - Frame the camera or primary viewpoint so the important geometry or data is visible immediately.
  - Use solution-appropriate lighting, materials, colors, or shader output so depth and structure are readable.
  - Include animation or interactivity that is frame-rate independent or otherwise bounded.
  - Show how external assets are loaded, preloaded, streamed, inlined, or replaced by placeholders on failure.
  - Handle resize, device pixel ratio, touch input, and constrained mobile or low-power performance.
  - Include the performance strategy expected for this solution, such as instancing, batching, LOD, streaming, server rendering, or shape-count limits.
